     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div>Hi,<br><br></div>I don&#39;t know if it&#39;s planned to add this natively, but you can already take inspiration on <a href=\"https://github.com/RCura/ScattRplot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/RCura/ScattRplot&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399444131000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OI4RtFIzybjrfH9QDEKWb\">this fork I made</a>, that allows selected values to be returned to R. See it working <a href=\"http://shiny.parisgeo.cnrs.fr/ScattRplot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.parisgeo.cnrs.fr/ScattRplot/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399444131000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dOhc5Zy45CeItCA7ZdlNT\">there</a> :)<br><br></div><div>This little proof of concept start to get old, I&#39;d rather look at <a href=\"http://www.htmlwidgets.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.htmlwidgets.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399444131000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2xPMzb3BjpofdapF09OTvS\">htmlwidgets</a> now to do the same thing.<br></div><div><br></div>HTH,<br><br></div>Robin<br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
